  "scope": [
    "The two actual turning roots are in the same original open tail, hence so is the entire closed positive gap. The symmetric argument uses the exact departure/arrival model numbers.",
    "The exact R11aRetainedCoordinates certificate supplies one existing order isomorphism, tail dilation and saturated cell inclusion. Its old and floored cellIndex identities imply the required index inequality.",
    "The final bounds use the same P, selected tail, Gamma, material datum, actual physical dilation and sample. All constants precede tail side, model number, point and sample cell.",
    "No supplied final material estimate, optical root lower bound, whole-gap single-cell condition, alternative Gamma or arbitrary Through03 retention is used.",
    "These results cover the actual two-tail Morse gaps. Identification of every whole positive component, including the two finite central gaps, remains separate."
  ]
